sentences.l:
But he, Zeus-sprung Odysseus, all the sorrows he had set
upon men and all he himself, suffering distress, toiled through,
all he was telling;

and how to Laestrygonian Telepylus he came,
who ships destroyed and the well-greaved companions,
all of them;

and how of the thronging Sirens the voice he heard,
and how he came to the Wandering Rocks and dread Charybdis
and Scylla, whom never yet uninjured men escaped;

and how the swift ship struck with a smoky thunderbolt
Zeus, high-thundering, and perished away the good companions
all together, but he himself the evil death-fates escaped;
